{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0019","type":"heading","page":1,"text":"When does admission for B.Tech programs begin?","bbox":null,"level":3,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0020","type":"paragraph","page":1,"text":"The admission to B.Tech programs begins in May-June.","bbox":null,"level":null,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0021","type":"heading","page":1,"text":"What is the admission criteria for B.Tech. programs?","bbox":null,"level":3,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0022","type":"paragraph","page":1,"text":"Admission to the undergraduate program of the DSPM IIIT-NR is based strictly on the merit of the candidate as inferred from their performance in JEE (Joint Entrance Examination). The minimum eligibility for applying for the B.Tech program under Chhattisgarh quota at IIIT-NR is 50% aggregate marks in Physics and Mathematics (45% for SC/ST/OBC/PWD candidates) in their 12th standard examination. The eligibility for applying for the B.Tech program under All India category and NTPC quota is as per JoSAA guidelines.","bbox":null,"level":null,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0023","type":"heading","page":1,"text":"Is Ph.D. offered at IIIT-NR?","bbox":null,"level":3,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0024","type":"paragraph","page":1,"text":"Yes. Please visit Admission section at our website for further details.","bbox":null,"level":null,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0025","type":"heading","page":1,"text":"When does admission for Ph.D. programs begin?","bbox":null,"level":3,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0026","type":"paragraph","page":1,"text":"The admission for Ph.D. programs usually takes place at the beginning of each semester (i.e June for Autumn semester and December for Spring semester)","bbox":null,"level":null,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0027","type":"heading","page":1,"text":"Is ragging prohibited in IIIT-NR?","bbox":null,"level":3,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0028","type":"paragraph","page":1,"text":"Ragging of any kind is strictly prohibited in the Institution. As per the directions of the Hon'ble Supreme Court of India, if any incident of ragging comes to the notice of the authorities, the concerned student will be given liberty to explain and if his explanation is not found satisfactory, he or she will be expelled from the Institution.","bbox":null,"level":null,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0029","type":"heading","page":1,"text":"Are there any scholarships available for B.Tech students?","bbox":null,"level":3,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0030","type":"heading","page":1,"text":"Are there any seats reserved for female candidates?","bbox":null,"level":3,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0031","type":"paragraph","page":1,"text":"For admission to its programs under CG Quota , the institute follows the Chhattisgarh State Government policy on reservation of 30% to Women. However , for admission under All India Quota & NTPC , Government of India policy on reservation applies.","bbox":null,"level":null,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0032","type":"heading","page":1,"text":"What are the documents required to be submitted at the time of admission?","bbox":null,"level":3,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0033","type":"paragraph","page":1,"text":"Please follow instructions available on the website as part of the application process.","bbox":null,"level":null,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
