{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0035","type":"paragraph","page":1,"text":"Please see the Admission Brochure.","bbox":null,"level":null,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0036","type":"heading","page":1,"text":"What is the strength of faculty?","bbox":null,"level":3,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0037","type":"paragraph","page":1,"text":"The Institute currently has 27 regular faculty members, with more joining in July 2019. In addition , there are adjunct and visiting faculty members too.","bbox":null,"level":null,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0038","type":"heading","page":1,"text":"Is hostel facility available? Are day-scholars allowed?","bbox":null,"level":3,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0039","type":"paragraph","page":1,"text":"Yes, there are three Boys hostels and one Girls hostel. All programs offered by IIIT-NR are fully residential. It is mandatory for all students to stay on campus, even if the student is from the Naya Raipur region. Hostel facilities for 1025 students (785 boys & 240 girls) are currently available.","bbox":null,"level":null,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0040","type":"heading","page":1,"text":"What is minimum cut-off for application to B.Tech. programs?","bbox":null,"level":3,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0041","type":"paragraph","page":1,"text":"There is no minimum cut-off of JEE Main Merit rankings.","bbox":null,"level":null,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0042","type":"heading","page":1,"text":"Will IIIT Naya Raipur admission happen through JoSAA?","bbox":null,"level":3,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0043","type":"paragraph","page":1,"text":"Yes w.e.f from 2017. Kindly visit JoSAA website at institute code 420. Admission through JoSAA is for All India Quota ( 35% seats).","bbox":null,"level":null,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0044","type":"heading","page":1,"text":"When will online applications for admission begin?","bbox":null,"level":3,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0045","type":"paragraph","page":1,"text":"Refer to the schedule announced.","bbox":null,"level":null,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0046","type":"heading","page":1,"text":"Can I apply under both All India quota and Chhattishgarh state quota?","bbox":null,"level":3,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0047","type":"paragraph","page":1,"text":"Yes, through JoSAA in case of All India quota and through our web portal if you are eligible under Chhattishgarh state quota.","bbox":null,"level":null,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0048","type":"heading","page":1,"text":"What is the best chance of getting a seat at IIIT-NR while choice filling in JoSAA portal?","bbox":null,"level":3,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0049","type":"paragraph","page":1,"text":"Select the choice of programs available at IIIT-NR (Institute code 420) as first ,second and Third choices.","bbox":null,"level":null,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0050","type":"heading","page":1,"text":"What is Admission under other categories?","bbox":null,"level":3,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0051","type":"paragraph","page":1,"text":"Other categories mean admissions under a) 50 % seats under Chhattishgarh State Quota b) 15 % seats under NTPC quota.","bbox":null,"level":null,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0052","type":"heading","page":1,"text":"How do I apply under State quota?","bbox":null,"level":3,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0053","type":"paragraph","page":1,"text":"After initial login at our admission portal, you will be asked to fill the requisite form.","bbox":null,"level":null,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0054","type":"heading","page":1,"text":"Is there any fee for application? If so, how to pay?","bbox":null,"level":3,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0055","type":"paragraph","page":1,"text":"Yes, candidates have to pay Rs.500/- online through admission portal.","bbox":null,"level":null,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0056","type":"heading","page":1,"text":"Can I fill choices without application fee?","bbox":null,"level":3,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0057","type":"paragraph","page":1,"text":"No. You will be able fill in choices only after successful fee payment.","bbox":null,"level":null,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0058","type":"heading","page":1,"text":"How should I order the choices of academic programs?","bbox":null,"level":3,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0059","type":"paragraph","page":1,"text":"You must fill your choices of academic program in the DECREASING order of preferences. That is, your most preferred one should be on the top.","bbox":null,"level":null,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0060","type":"heading","page":1,"text":"Will a candidate be allowed to reshuffle the choice list at any stage of seat allotment?","bbox":null,"level":3,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0061","type":"paragraph","page":1,"text":"Candidates are allowed to reshuffle/reorder their choices ONLY during choice filling period before they “lock” their choices. Beyond that there is NO option of reordering.","bbox":null,"level":null,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0062","type":"heading","page":1,"text":"What is locking of choices? Once locked, can I unlock?","bbox":null,"level":3,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0063","type":"paragraph","page":1,"text":"Lock is an option indicating the finalization of choices. Choices will be automatically locked on the last date of application.","bbox":null,"level":null,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0064","type":"heading","page":1,"text":"What is the period of choice filling?","bbox":null,"level":3,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0065","type":"paragraph","page":1,"text":"Refer to the schedule announced.","bbox":null,"level":null,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0066","type":"heading","page":1,"text":"Is there any cut off marks for registration and choice?","bbox":null,"level":3,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0067","type":"paragraph","page":1,"text":"Yes, The eligibility for applying for the B.Tech program under Chhattisgarh quota at IIIT-NR is 50% aggregate marks in Physics and Mathematics (45% for SC/ST/OBC/PWD candidates) in their 12th standard examination. The eligibility for applying for the B.Tech program under All India category and NTPC quota is as per JoSAA guidelines.","bbox":null,"level":null,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0068","type":"heading","page":1,"text":"How many rounds of seat allotment will happen?","bbox":null,"level":3,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0069","type":"paragraph","page":1,"text":"Three rounds","bbox":null,"level":null,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0070","type":"heading","page":1,"text":"What if seats remain vacant after three rounds? Will they be filled on quota or category basis?","bbox":null,"level":3,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
{"id":"general-institute_faqs:e0071","type":"paragraph","page":1,"text":"Seats remaining vacant at the end of three rounds of counseling, under any quota or reserved category shall be converted to All-India General(Open) and shall be available for admissions in the Spot Round.","bbox":null,"level":null,"table":null,"reader":"markdown","confidence":null,"order":0,"attrs":{},"status":"extracted","reasons":[]}
